    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1006">

                <pb facs="0977" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.105/45</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Mayer to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-06T10:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 6, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the request of General Butler Legation respectfully solicits Department to use
                    good offices to expedite modification of gendarmerie agreement, substituting two
                    lieutenants for one inspector Coast <pb facs="0978" n="812" xml:id="pg812"/>
                    Guard as per correspondence contained in letter dated November third from chief
                    gendarmerie to brigade commander Haiti forwarded to headquarters Marine
                    Corps.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
